# Payment safety (Live activated)

Production: **`LIVE_PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true`** (Stripe runtime LIVE). Payment architecture is **PRODUCTION-FROZEN** (see `00-payment-production-freeze.mdc`).

Do not flip the kill switch off except as an emergency after a verified Live money invariant failure. TEST history stays operable via mode-scoped clients. Do not change Live flags as a side effect of UI, fee, ticket, test, deploy, or env cleanup.

## PCI

Never put raw PAN/CVC in scripts, APIs, or tests. Browser cards: Stripe.js / Payment Element. Automated Stripe: official TEST PaymentMethod IDs, mocks, or fixtures.

## Connect

Sourcer/seller destination = **that user’s own** Connect account (`txn.sellerId` / `ticket.sellerId`). Never default other sellers to a historical Connect account. Buyers do not need Connect merely to buy.

## QA

Do not create PaymentIntent / Charge / Transfer / Refund / payout unless the task explicitly requires Live (or TEST-history) financial verification. Ordinary ticket/UI work: no Stripe money objects.

## Guard

`npm run test:live-guard` must pass (source default remains false; Production env is true). Do not change Live flags except an explicit emergency or Live-ops task.
